  var input = document.querySelector("input[type=text]");
  var button = document.querySelector("button");
  button.addEventListener("click", function() {
    var value = input.value;
    alert(value);
  });
});
```
This code is injected into a website's source code. When a user visits the website, the code is executed. It captures the user's login credentials and displays them in an alert box.

To protect against malicious code, websites should regularly update their software and scan their code for vulnerabilities. Users should also be careful when entering sensitive information on websites.

